From: TrinityXSX <trinityxsx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:53:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] TrinityXSX: limit Web Companion PIN guesses

Anyone on the same Wi-Fi could try all 10^6 PINs and then edit
xcl.toml, game_paths.txt or saves. After 5 distinct wrong PINs the
companion now refuses PIN checks for 30 s, doubling per further wrong
PIN up to 10 min (429 + Retry-After); even the right PIN is refused
while locked, so a guesser learns nothing.

- The count is global (a LAN client picks its own address) and a
  correct PIN does not reset it (the dashboard polls every 3 s).
- Only distinct wrong PINs count, so a dashboard tab left open from
  before a restart (old PIN) costs one try instead of locking the new
  session; the dashboard also stops auto-refresh on 403/429.
- Requests without a PIN only get the login page and are not counted.
- Constant-time PIN compare; PIN mixes in OS-seeded RandomState.
